00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you?
-Good. I'm impressed.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm well.
I'm impressed with your energy

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.138 line:92%
-You bet. Today's a good day

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:09.342
-You had a good day becaus
one of your former, I guess,

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
competitors for the nomination
Julian Castro,

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:12.712 line:92%
endorsed you this morning.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, he did.
-That's really nice.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It really is.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:19.119
-It must be particularly nice to
get an endorsement from someon

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
who, you know,
has shared a stage with you,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.356
has gone through the first few
months of this process with you.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you find out about
something like that happening?

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.495 line:92%
-Well, you know, Julian and

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
have been friends
for a long time,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we fight
for a lot of the same things

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has this remarkable story
about his life

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how he ended up
in public service.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And we're out there

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:43.376
fighting for people who don'
have a voice in our government

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.677 line:92%
You know, we both see an America

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's working great if you're
rich, if you're powerful,

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you have an army of lawyers
and lobbyists.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's not working so grea
for everybody else.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:57.657
And we feel like we've got thi
chance in 2020, this real chance

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:01.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be able to build an America
that works for everybody.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Julian is just -- just
a great partner in this fight.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, you mention partner,
because, of course,

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
anytime anyone
endorses someone else,

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
they go, "Oh, potential
running mate."

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.637 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What do you have to --

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.337 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Way too presumptuous

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be talking about
that sort of thing.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you don't
rush into things.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to go slow
with stuff like that.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.212 line:92%
I want to talk about someone

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're both,
I believe, fans of.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's her birthday today --
Kate McKinnon,

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
who does an impression
of you on "SNL."

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:28.955 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
And I was wondering --

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was wondering how you feel
about the impression.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:33.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is it like seeing yoursel
on "Saturday Night Live"?

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:33.993 line:92%
How do you feel Kate's doing

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.497 size:88% position:44%
-You know, I have to say
she is really fabulous.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.733 line:92%
She's smart. She's engaged

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, she brings
a lot of energy.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.605 line:92%
We wear the same jackets.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to give credit --
I want to do give quick credit

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the "SNL" wardrobe
department,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:53.179
who makes more jackets than yo
can believe to match candidates.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's exactly right.
She does great.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.884 line:92%
And, look, here's the deal

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
Elect me President
of the United States,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:00.887 line:92%
and we get eight more year

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Kate McKinnon
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.959 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.694 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know, I --

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:11.030
I played John Kerry, and I think
it worked against him.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:11.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:12.732 line:92%
I think it worked against him.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just got to say, Seth,
I know John Kerry.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.704 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You're no Kate McKinnon.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very --
That is very fair.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the things, as you figh
big money in politics,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
as you fight
corruption in politics,

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:30.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
you stay away from big donors,
large-dollar donors.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:31.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you have
smaller-dollar donors.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:36.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you sort of famously
call a lot of them personally.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.056 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.358 line:92%
-But I would have to imagine

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
